1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
One sky. The Chinese saw — a turtle
entwined with a snake.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Guardian of the north — and of winter,
water and death. Its stars: seven lunar
mansions.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,000
After dark, the seven arc from Dou, the
Southern Dipper, in the south…

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:23,000
…to Shi and Bi in the east: the Room and
the Wall.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Just north lies Tengshe, “the Flying
Serpent.” Turtle and snake, one still,
one moving, make Xuanwu.

6
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Two stars of the Room, two of the Wall:
in the West, the Great Square of
Pegasus.

7
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:48,000
South of the Square camps Yulinjun,
“Feathered Forest Guard” — 45 stars.

8
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Fomalhaut stands out low in the autumn
south. In Chinese, Beiluo Shimen: “gate
of the northern camp.”

9
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Dragon in the east, turtle and snake in
the north, tiger in the west, bird in
the south.

10
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Mid-Autumn: where the Moon rests.

11
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:11,000
Follow for a new sky every week.

